^A is somewhat buggy in NetHack 3.4.3.

In the unstable development version of NetHack 4, I've generalized ^A,
and removed most of the issues with it (although it still has problems
repeating spell letters, at the moment). It now has the general
semantics of "repeat the last action or continue an interrupted action".
For instance, if you type 20s, then get interrupted after 5 turns (say
by a distant explosion), pressing ^A will search for another 15 turns.

